            "answer": {
              "short": "$1320$ ways.",
              "worked": "There are ${}^{8}P_4$ unrestricted teams. For an unacceptable team, include Marcus and Sophie, choose two others in ${}^{6}C_2$ ways, then arrange the four runners in $4!$ ways.\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}N&={}^{8}P_4-{}^{6}C_2\\times4!\\\\N&=1680-15\\times24\\\\N&=1320\\end{aligned}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 23
          },
          {
            "id": "p85-q1-b-ii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "ii",
            "prompt": "Without using combinations.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$1320$ ways.",
              "worked": "For an unacceptable team, choose one of 4 positions for Marcus, one of the remaining 3 positions for Sophie, then fill the remaining 2 positions from the other 6 students.\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}N&={}^{8}P_4-4\\times3\\times{}^{6}P_2\\\\N&=1680-4\\times3\\times30\\\\N&=1320\\end{aligned}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
